llowing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The essence of the issue mentioned in https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12382 and https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/6709 is that manual assignment when bone estimation fails is cumbersome.\r\n\r\nI'm skeptical about this PR's approach if it want to address the issue, because it's too narrow in scope and lacks reusability; Specifically, it is necessary to precisely specify the symbols for distinguishing left and right, and it cannot be applied to spine bones.\r\n\r\nTherefore, I suggest implementing a process where manual assignment is followed by manually executing bone estimation based on those assignments. That approach would allows for the reuse of the existing bone estimation method that utilizes RegEx for left/right determination which has been already included.","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115122#pullrequestreview-3677516642","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115122","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115122#pullrequestreview-3677516642"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115122"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-19T11:03:06Z","commit_id":"f2b932f9f0ee72e00b361d575664c4be2c1da133"}]